  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scVI_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) achieved 0.650 accuracy, a large jump over config_004 (scVI_n200, singleprofile) at 0.520, confirming that multi-profile with aggregation is highly beneficial. However, we only have one data point on aggregation (avgpool). Uncertainty: it is unknown whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) further improves over simple average pooling, or whether avgpool already captures most of the multi-profile benefit. This experiment (config_006: scVI_n200, multiprofile, transformer) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005—only the aggregation changes. It directly isolates the effect of aggregation method while holding encoder and profile setting fixed. Under a limited budget, resolving whether transformer aggregation adds value over avgpool is critical because the answer propagates to every future multimodal or multiprofile experiment, making this the highest-information next step."
}

